.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In the last of his 1905 papers, Einstein showed that a body&#x27;s rest mass and rest energy are the same quantity, E_0=mc^2 -- the rest-frame special case of the fully relativistic relation E^2=(pc)^2+(mc^2)^2. FourVector builds exactly this object, with its .mass property returning the invariant \sqrt{E^2-|\vec p|^2}. This example checks that the invariant mass a moving observer computes agrees exactly with the rest energy measured in the particle&#x27;s own rest frame -- true at every boost velocity, however fast -- and that summing four-vectors before taking the mass, rather than after, is what makes invariant mass differ from simply adding up individual particle masses.">

